# Hinglish voice assistant: what we are building

Oct 4, 2026 · @Harshit

## Summary

A personal voice assistant in the spirit of Jarvis. You speak to it in Hinglish, it answers aloud in about a second, it remembers your preferences, and it takes actions through tools. Every model in the main path is open-weight, fine-tuned or tuned by you, and served from one GPU server you run.

The point of the project is the measured engineering behind it: fine-tuning, quantisation and model serving, each with numbers, inside a product a recruiter can talk to.

## What the user experiences

> **You:** "Kal subah 7 baje ka alarm laga do, aur ghar ke liye doodh aur bread order kar do."
>
> **Assistant:** "Alarm set ho gaya. Instamart pe doodh aur bread ₹112 ka hai, usual address pe. Order kar doon?"
>
> **You:** "Haan."

- **Natural speech.** Hindi, English and the mix of both, in one sentence.
- **Fast replies.** It starts speaking before the full answer is written.
- **Interruptible.** If you talk over it, it stops and listens.
- **Remembers you.** Address, diet, usual brands, routines, and new facts it picks up in conversation.
- **Acts for you.** Orders, reminders, calendar entries, web lookups, notes.
- **Asks before it spends.** Anything that costs money or sends a message is read back and needs a spoken yes.

